   character for character. Real `show interface` prints prose like
   `current duplex full, current speed 1000, current polarity mdix`; `show interface
   status` prints aligned COLUMNS (`a-full`, `a-1000`, `connected`/`notconnect`).
   Machine-style tokens (`speed=1000`, `duplex=full`, `state=up`) DO NOT EXIST and make
   the test fail on working hardware. AW+ port names have the form `portX.Y.Z`, never
   `1/0/1`. If the reference does not show the output you need, assert on a substring you
   can see in it — do not guess a format.
   **A port name is CLI TEXT, never a Python identifier.** It may appear only inside a
   string (`dut.cmd('interface {}'.format(port))`); writing it as an attribute —
   `self.dut.port1.0.1` — is a SyntaxError.
